E["npc:bloodmage-drazial"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Drazial",z="blastedlands",s="At the northern pass, Bloodmage Drazial studies the Blasted Lands with his sister Lynnore. They examine its native beasts and brew mixtures for hardy travelers.",h="At the northern pass, Bloodmage Drazial studies the Blasted Lands with his sister Lynnore.",sec={{t="Alchemical Studies in the Red Wastes",b="Near the northern pass between the Swamp of Sorrows and the Blasted Lands, Bloodmage Drazial studies a strange magic. He and his sister Lynnore draw power from the harsh land through blood magic. Many high elves reject such forbidden arts or grieve for Quel'Thalas.\n\nScorpoks, snickerfangs, and blasted boars thrive with unnatural vigor. Drazial and Lynnore believe the Dark Portal's opening released the energy that changed them. They gather the beasts' organs and tissues, then brew volatile mixtures that grant great strength, agility, and endurance.",sp=0},{t="An Independent Supplier",b="Drazial works apart from the factions stationed in the Blasted Lands. He serves neither the Alliance nor the Horde. Instead, he trades his alchemical skill to anyone hardy enough to cross the wasteland and gather his ingredients. Travelers bring organs from local predators, and his cauldrons keep bubbling.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Drazial?",a="Near the Blasted Lands' northern entrance, Bloodmage Drazial studies local wildlife and brews alchemical reagents. He is a blood elf mage who works with his sister Lynnore, using parts from corrupted beasts.",al={"who is drazial","drazial lore","bloodmage drazial npc"}},{q="Why is Drazial collecting animal parts?",a="The Blasted Lands' creatures have adapted to blighted, magically charged terrain. Drazial uses potent organs from boars, hyenas, scorpions, and basilisks to brew elixirs that strengthen a warrior's body.",al={"why does drazial want boar lungs","drazial quest items","drazial animal organs"}},{q="Does Drazial work for the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Drazial is neutral toward both factions. He and Lynnore take no part in the war between Stormwind and the Horde. They deal with any traveler willing to supply their magical and alchemical research.",al={"drazial faction","is drazial horde or alliance","can alliance talk to drazial"}},{q="Who is the other blood elf camped with him?",a="Bloodmage Lynnore is the blood elf camped beside Drazial, and she is his sister. Together they practice blood magic and brew different mixtures from beasts roaming the Blasted Lands.",al={"drazial companion","who is with drazial","lynnore"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how Drazial's craft departs from traditional Kirin Tor spellcraft. He uses blood magic and biological reagents to make arcane enhancements."},kw={"blasted boar","blasted lands","bloodmage","concoctions","drazial","lynnore","scorpok","snickerfang"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Bloodmage Drazial"}}
E["npc:bloodmage-lynnore"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Lynnore",z="blastedlands",s="Near the Blasted Lands' northern entrance, Bloodmage Lynnore studies the power within local beasts. She camps with her brother Drazial and brews draughts from their organs.",h="Near the Blasted Lands' northern entrance, Bloodmage Lynnore studies the power within local beasts.",sec={{t="Master of Blood Magic",b="Near the northern entrance to the Blasted Lands, Bloodmage Lynnore studies blood magic with her brother Drazial. Few elves in the Eastern Kingdoms practice this forbidden art. The land is harsh and corrupting, yet Lynnore searches native beasts for arcane and vital energies. Travelers bring her brains and gizzards from local animals. She distills them into elixirs that sharpen intellect and spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Lynnore?",a="Bloodmage Lynnore is a blood elf blood mage camped near the Blasted Lands' northern entrance. Travelers bring her beast parts for powerful concoctions that enhance their abilities.",al={"who is lynnore","bloodmage lynnore lore","lynnore blasted lands"}},{q="Where can Bloodmage Lynnore be found?",a="Lynnore camps with her brother, Bloodmage Drazial, near the Blasted Lands' northern entrance. Their camp lies where the pass from the Swamp of Sorrows opens onto the wastes.",al={"lynnore location","where is lynnore","how to find bloodmage lynnore"}},{q="What concoctions does she brew?",a="Lynnore brews rare tonics from local wildlife, including basilisk brains, vulture gizzards, and snickerfang jowls. Her Cerebral Cortex Compound and Gizzard Gum enhance intellect and spirit for a long time.",al={"lynnore buffs","blasted lands consumables","cerebral cortex compound"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you can trade with Lynnore in the Blasted Lands. She offers unique concoctions to anyone from either faction who brings her the raw ingredients.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage drawn to unconventional spellcraft, you can look to Lynnore's rare and controversial arcane path. She manipulates vital essence instead of conventional ley energies."},kw={"blasted lands","blood magic","bloodmage lynnore","cerebral cortex compound","gizzard gum","lynnore"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:horde"},src={"Bloodmage Lynnore"}}
E["npc:thadius-grimshade"] = {t="npc",n="Thadius Grimshade",z="blastedlands",s="At Nethergarde Keep, Thadius Grimshade seeks knowledge in divination and darker magic. Though long gone from Aerie Peak, he remains loyal to his kin.",h="At Nethergarde Keep, Thadius Grimshade seeks knowledge in divination and darker magic.",sec={{t="A Wildhammer in the Wastes",b="Thadius Grimshade lives within Nethergarde Keep, far from the open skies and roaring winds favored by most Wildhammer dwarves. He came to the edge of the tainted Blasted Lands to study arcane divination and darker mystic lore. Though apart from his clan, he still cherishes his homeland and gryphonkind. When folk from Aerie Peak seek his aid, he offers his rare skill in scrying.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Divination",b="When Gryphon Master Talonaxe seeks the captured gryphon Sharpbeak, Thadius performs a divination ritual with one of the beast's feathers. For his aid, he demands the medallion worn by the troll necromancer Nekrum Gutchewer. Thadius seeks its secret of unnatural longevity while trying to avoid its corrupting harm. With the medallion, he pierces the veil of Jintha'Alor and reveals where Sharpbeak is held.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thadius Grimshade?",a="Thadius Grimshade is a Wildhammer dwarf mage and diviner at Nethergarde Keep. He left his mountain home to study darker, unorthodox magic far to the south.",al={"thadius grimshade","who is thadius","thadius npc"}},{q="Where can Thadius Grimshade be found?",a="Thadius Grimshade lives inside the high wizard tower at Nethergarde Keep, an Alliance stronghold in the northern Blasted Lands.",al={"thadius location","where is thadius grimshade","thadius blasted lands"}},{q="Why does he want Nekrum's Medallion?",a="Thadius wants the medallion carried by Nekrum Gutchewer to learn how its magic grants long life and seek that longevity without suffering its sinister side effects.",al={"nekrums medallion thadius","why thadius wants medallion","nekrum gutchewer medallion"}},{q="How does he help find Sharpbeak?",a="Thadius uses a feather shed by the missing gryphon and Nekrum's Medallion in a scrying ritual. It reveals Sharpbeak is held at the heights of Jintha'Alor in the Hinterlands.",al={"thadius sharpbeak","divining sharpbeak","finding sharpbeak quest"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may find Thadius an oddity among the Wildhammers. Rather than soar on gryphons, he spends his years in arcane study inside a human fortress.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage visiting Nethergarde, you may recognize Thadius's rare methods of divination. He studies troll relics in hopes of mastering longevity magic."},kw={"blasted lands","diviner","nekrum gutchewer","nethergarde keep","sharpbeak","thadius grimshade","wildhammer"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","zone:hinterlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Thadius Grimshade"}}
E["subzone:dark-portal"] = {t="subzone",n="Dark Portal",z="blastedlands",s="At the Blasted Lands' southern rim, the dormant Dark Portal holds a rift between worlds. Its opening brought the Old Horde into Azeroth and began the First War.",h="At the Blasted Lands' southern rim, the dormant Dark Portal holds a rift between worlds.",sec={{t="A Rift Across Realities",b="Where the Black Morass once spread across the south, the Dark Portal tore open. Medivh, possessed by Sargeras, joined his Tirisfal magics with Gul'dan's fel sorcery on Draenor. Their ritual drained countless lives and ripped reality apart. The Old Horde anchored the rift with massive stonework, then marched through to shatter the Kingdom of Stormwind in the First War.\n\nFel power from the portal poisoned the land. Lush marshes became the red, petrified wastes you see today.",sp=0},{t="Dormant Vigilance",b="After the Alliance of Lordaeron won the Second War, Archmage Khadgar shattered the portal's stone frame with powerful magic. He hoped to sever Draenor from Azeroth forever, but the tear beneath it proved impossible to destroy. The Alliance built Nethergarde Keep nearby to watch the scar.\n\nDemons and remnants of the Shadow Council still creep through the blasted caldera. The gateway has been reassembled, yet remains dormant. It is a silent wound between worlds that neither side dares abandon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can you walk through the Dark Portal right now?",a="No. The Dark Portal's stone frame is intact, but the rift within lies dormant. No traveler can cross it now.",al={"can i enter the dark portal","is dark portal open","portal to outland"}},{q="Who originally built the Dark Portal?",a="Medivh, the human Guardian on Azeroth, and Gul'dan, the warlock on Draenor, joined in a ritual to create the Dark Portal. Their work set in motion the invasion that began the First War.",al={"who created dark portal","medivh guldan portal","dark portal creators"}},{q="Why does Nethergarde Keep watch over it?",a="After Archmage Khadgar shattered the portal's first frame following the Second War, he persuaded the Alliance to watch its ruins. The Alliance founded Nethergarde Keep to keep watch in case threats returned.",al={"why is nethergarde keep here","nethergarde portal watch","why nethergarde"}},{q="Why is the ground around the portal red and barren?",a="The Blasted Lands were once the fertile Black Morass. Fel magic used to tear reality, corruption from Draenor, and demonic beasts poisoned the soil and petrified the land.",al={"why are blasted lands dead","portal corruption","why is blasted lands red"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For your people, the Dark Portal marks a painful past. Under demonic masters, the Old Horde marched through it and left their ancestral homeland for war.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Dark Portal recalls the First War and the fall of ancient Stormwind. The mages of Nethergarde keep watch over it without end."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dark portal","draenor","great portal","guldan","khadgar","medivh"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:nethergarde-keep","topic:medivh","topic:old-horde","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:burning-legion","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron"},src={"Dark Portal"}}
E["subzone:dreadmaul-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmaul Post",z="blastedlands",s="Ogres hold Dreadmaul Post near the Dark Portal. The Dreadmaul clan raised this fortified settlement in the Blasted Lands after crossing from Draenor. Travelers face the ogres and the harsh wastes around their camp.",h="Ogres hold Dreadmaul Post near the Dark Portal.",sec={{t="Remnants of Draenor",b="The Dreadmaul clan crossed into Azeroth with the Horde decades ago. Near the Dark Portal, they raised rough stone mounds and earthworks in the Blasted Lands’ red wastes. Dreadmaul Post is one of their chief outposts. From here, the ogres hold the badlands and clash with wandering beasts and travelers who approach their territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Dreadmaul Post?",a="The Dreadmaul clan of ogres lives at Dreadmaul Post. They crossed from Draenor through the Dark Portal during the wars and made a lasting home in the Blasted Lands’ desolate crags.",al={"who is at dreadmaul post","dreadmaul post inhabitants","dreadmaul ogres"}},{q="Why are the ogres still in the Blasted Lands?",a="After the Old Horde fell and the Dark Portal was sealed, many ogres scattered across Azeroth. The Dreadmaul clan stayed near the place where they first entered and made the scarred wastes around the dormant rift their home.",al={"why dreadmaul here","ogres blasted lands","why ogres near portal"}},{q="Who else wanders the area near the post?",a="Scorpid and basilisks prowl the red desert near Dreadmaul Post, along with the ogres.",al={"draenei blasted lands","who is near dreadmaul","creatures dreadmaul post"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Dreadmaul once fought beside the Old Horde, but wild clans like theirs have broken with Thrall’s new order. They regard every traveler as a hostile invader.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance scouts watching the Dark Portal, the Dreadmaul ogres are a violent, entrenched danger. Their presence makes patrols through the continent’s southern reaches harder."},kw={"blasted lands","dark portal","dreadmaul","dreadmaul post","ogre mound","ogres"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:dark-portal"},src={"Dreadmaul Post"}}
E["subzone:garrison-armory"] = {t="subzone",n="Garrison Armory",z="blastedlands",s="Alliance miners work the Garrison Armory southwest of Nethergarde Keep. Their ore supplies the fortress and brings wealth to Stormwind.",h="Alliance miners work the Garrison Armory southwest of Nethergarde Keep.",sec={{t="A Lifeline in the Red Wastes",b="Nethergarde Keep must hold its watch over the Dark Portal, and long supply trains from Stormwind cannot meet every need. In the Garrison Armory’s underground mine shafts, miners work under foremen with engineers at their side. Ore mined there goes to Nethergarde’s smiths and fortifications, or travels to Stormwind in trade for food, tools, and other provisions the keep needs.",sp=0},{t="Vulnerable Industry",b="The Garrison Armory lies beyond Nethergarde Keep’s main walls, exposed to the red desert’s dangers. Dreadmaul ogres and wild beasts prowl the surrounding crags. Armed guards protect the workers in the tunnels, for any disruption to the mine threatens the keep’s watch over the blasted frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Garrison Armory used for?",a="Workers at Nethergarde Keep mine metal and minerals in the Garrison Armory. The ore supplies the fortress and is traded to Stormwind for food and equipment.",al={"garrison armory purpose","what is this mine","why is there a mine here"}},{q="Who works in the armory?",a="Nethergarde miners, engineers, and foremen work in the armory. They excavate ore and maintain the shafts under Nethergarde’s command.",al={"who is inside","armory npcs","garrison miners"}},{q="Why does Nethergarde Keep need this mine?",a="Nethergarde Keep stands isolated in the desolate Blasted Lands, where regular supply lines are difficult. The mine provides metal to repair gear and reinforce defenses. Excess materials can be traded to Stormwind for vital supplies.",al={"why nethergarde needs it","armory importance","nethergarde resources"}},{q="Can Horde players enter the Garrison Armory?",a="The Garrison Armory is held by hostile Alliance workers and guards. Horde adventurers still brave its depths to claim rich ore from the mine shafts.",al={"can horde go here","horde in garrison armory","is it safe for horde"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Valuable mineral veins run through the rugged stone beneath the Garrison Armory, making its mine shafts a contested quarry.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Armory’s workforce labors constantly to keep Nethergarde Keep supplied with weapons, armor, and trade goods for its lonely watch."},kw={"blasted lands","garrison armory","mine","nethergarde","nethergarde engineer","nethergarde keep","nethergarde miner","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Garrison Armory"}}
E["subzone:nethergarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Nethergarde Keep",z="blastedlands",s="Nethergarde Keep watches the Dark Portal from the bluffs above the road into the Blasted Lands. The Alliance raised it after the Second War to guard the dormant gateway and the red wastes beyond. Mages and soldiers, supplied by Stormwind, keep watch against demons and lingering corruption.",h="Nethergarde Keep watches the Dark Portal from the bluffs above the road into the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Sentinel Against the Red World",b="After the Dark Portal fell at the end of the Second War, Archmage Khadgar and the Alliance of Lordaeron knew the rift could not go unguarded. So the Alliance raised bastions, barracks, and mage spires along the canyon pass into the Blasted Lands. Kirin Tor sorcerers took their posts in the keep. They watched the shattered gateway and wove wards to keep demonic blight from creeping north into the human kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="The Lonely Vigil",b="When the Dark Portal reopened, the Alliance Expedition crossed into Draenor. Khadgar and his companions sealed the gateway behind them, leaving Nethergarde to guard its silent remnant. For two decades, scholars from Dalaran and the Wizard's Sanctum have studied the portal's lingering energies, mutated local fauna, and demonic incursions.\n\nAfter Dalaran was ravaged during the Third War, Stormwind City became the keep's sole source of vital supply caravans. Its soldiers and mages now stand alone against the horrors haunting the wasteland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Nethergarde Keep built?",a="After the Second War, Archmage Khadgar and the Alliance of Lordaeron commissioned Nethergarde Keep to guard against another orcish invasion from Draenor and contain demonic corruption spreading through the Blasted Lands.",al={"purpose of nethergarde","why is nethergarde here","nethergarde history"}},{q="Who constructed the keep?",a="The Alliance of Lordaeron raised Nethergarde Keep at Archmage Khadgar's urging after the Second War. Wizards of Dalaran's Kirin Tor chiefly staffed it.",al={"who built nethergarde","nethergarde builders"}},{q="Who commands and supplies the fortress now?",a="Stormwind now provides Nethergarde Keep with troops, regular supply caravans, and logistical support. Dalaran's Kirin Tor once maintained the keep, but Dalaran fell to the Scourge and the Legion.",al={"who runs nethergarde","nethergarde supplies","stormwind nethergarde"}},{q="What are the mages inside the keep studying?",a="Researchers from the Wizard's Sanctum study the dormant energies of the Dark Portal, mutations afflicting local wildlife, and ways to ward off the fel taint lingering over the red landscape.",al={"nethergarde mages","wizards sanctum nethergarde","what are they researching"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know Nethergarde as a place where Kirin Tor mages have spent decades studying dimensional rifts, sealing them, and holding back fel corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Nethergarde as a forward stronghold built with blood and gold to keep the horrors of the First and Second Wars from passing through the portal again."},kw={"blasted lands","dark portal","keep","khadgar","kirin tor","nethergarde","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:dark-portal","zone:blastedlands","zone:stormwind","topic:second-war","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Nethergarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:serpent-s-coil"] = {t="subzone",n="Serpent's Coil",z="blastedlands",s="Dark cultists shelter in Serpent's Coil, among caves and burnt encampments in the eastern Blasted Lands. Scorched orcish ruins from older wars line the ridges.",h="Dark cultists shelter in Serpent's Coil, among caves and burnt encampments in the eastern Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Labyrinth of Ash and Stone",b="In the eastern Blasted Lands, Serpent's Coil winds through cliffs and old ruins. Its paths pass ruined orcish huts from the First and Second Wars. Shadowsworn cultists and practitioners of dark arts haunt the tunnels. Demonic energies lingering in the red wastes draw them there, beyond the watchful eyes of Nethergarde Keep.",sp=0},{t="The Cultist Lair",b="Archmage Allistarj's cultists have long used Serpent's Coil as a staging ground. They revere demonic lords and experiment with sinister artifacts such as the Amulet of Allistarj. Though their master's grasp weakens, loyal Shadowsworn zealots still patrol the cave turns. Behind scorched barricades, they keep rituals for Kirith the Damned.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Serpent's Coil?",a="Serpent's Coil winds through caves and a canyon in the eastern Blasted Lands, amid charred orcish ruins.",al={"serpents coil","what is this cave","blasted lands serpent coil"}},{q="Why are there old orc structures here?",a="The old encampments date to the First and Second Wars. The Old Horde crossed the nearby Dark Portal then and fortified the surrounding region before its defeat.",al={"why orc ruins","orc buildings blasted lands","burnt huts"}},{q="Who lives inside Serpent's Coil?",a="Shadowsworn cultists aligned with Archmage Allistarj occupy the caverns and serve demonic powers.",al={"who is here","serpent coil enemies","who controls the cave"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Warlock, you may recognize the Shadowsworn's binding rituals and potent artifacts as grim signs of reckless demonic study."},kw={"allistarj","blasted lands","kirith the damned","serpent's coil","serpents coil","shadowsworn"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Serpent's Coil"}}
E["subzone:tainted-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Tainted Scar",z="blastedlands",s="In the southwestern Blasted Lands, demons gather beneath Lord Kazzak’s command. Fel magic has made the Tainted Scar their stronghold.",h="In the southwestern Blasted Lands, demons gather beneath Lord Kazzak’s command.",sec={{t="A Bastion of the Legion",b="Where the Black Morass once spread, the Tainted Scar now cuts through the land as a lifeless trench stained like dried blood. Fel energies from the Dark Portal drained the wetlands and twisted the ground. After Archimonde fell at Mount Hyjal during the Third War, the surviving Burning Legion forces rallied in the south.\n\nThe colossal ered'ruin Lord Kazzak claimed the Scar for his stronghold. Elite demons hold its blackened rises, while lieutenants such as Razelikh the Defiler command the wasted red soil.",sp=0},{t="Unholy Inhabitants",b="Most mortals avoid the Tainted Scar, where death comes in agony. Yet fel energies draw those who practice the dark arts. Daio the Decrepit, an eccentric human warlock, lives beside a ruined demonic altar that overlooks the horrors.\n\nHe uses the fiends around him in dark rituals. There, he teaches aspiring warlocks to summon and bind dread infernals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tainted Scar?",a="The Tainted Scar cuts through the southwestern Blasted Lands, corrupted by demonic magic from the Dark Portal. Once part of the Black Morass, it withered into a barren, blood-red wasteland where high-ranking Burning Legion demons now dwell.",al={"what is tainted scar","tainted scar lore","why is the ground red here"}},{q="Who rules the Tainted Scar?",a="Lord Kazzak rules the Tainted Scar. After the Burning Legion's defeat in the Third War, the towering doomguard commander rallied the surviving demons in the south and keeps a deadly foothold on Azeroth.",al={"who leads the demons here","tainted scar boss","lord kazzak tainted scar"}},{q="Why is an old human living among the demons here?",a="Daio the Decrepit is an aged human warlock who lives among the demons to harness the Scar's potent fel energies. At a ruined demonic altar, he performs dark rituals and mentors seasoned warlocks in summoning infernals.",al={"who is daio","daio the decrepit","hermit in tainted scar"}},{q="Is the Tainted Scar connected to the Dark Portal?",a="Yes. When the Dark Portal first breached the boundary between worlds, chaotic Nether energies spilled into the surrounding swamps. The Tainted Scar absorbed much of this magic, twisting the land into an inhospitable demonic stronghold.",al={"tainted scar dark portal connection","why is it corrupted"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Veteran warlocks seek Daio the Decrepit at his demonic altar. There, they learn to enslave and command fiery infernals.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance commanders watch the canyon closely. They fear Lord Kazzak's entrenched demon army could surge north into the Swamp of Sorrows or Stormwind territory."},kw={"blasted lands","burning legion","daio the decrepit","eredruin","kazzak","lord kazzak","razelikh","tainted scar"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:burning-legion","subzone:dark-portal","topic:third-war","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Tainted Scar"}}
E["zone:blastedlands"] = {t="zone",n="Blasted Lands",z="blastedlands",s="In the Blasted Lands, Nethergarde Keep watches a wasteland scarred by the Dark Portal. Red clay and barren rock cover the former Black Morass, while demons and Dreadmaul ogres still threaten the region.",h="In the Blasted Lands, Nethergarde Keep watches a wasteland scarred by the Dark Portal.",sec={{t="A Scarred Wasteland",b="Once, the Blasted Lands belonged to the Black Morass, a stretch of dense fenland. During the First War, the warlock Gul'dan and the possessed Medivh tore open the Dark Portal and unleashed the orcish Horde. Fel energies poured through the breach. They drained the land of moisture and baked it into cracked red clay.\n\nThe Portal was destroyed at the end of the Second War. Its shockwaves scorched the ground again and turned the native stone crimson.",sp=0},{t="Nethergarde's Lonely Vigil",b="Nethergarde Keep watches the only road into the valley from the northern bluffs. Archmage Khadgar and the Kirin Tor commissioned the stone fortress after the Second War. Its mages and soldiers are sworn to stop renewed demonic or orcish incursions.\n\nThe posting is strict. Garrison members who break its rules are banished to the Stockade in Stormwind. Dreadmaul ogres remained after Draenor's fall and keep the defenders under pressure. They raid the roads and attack the gates under fell guidance.",sp=0},{t="The Legion's Remnant",b="The Tainted Scar cuts through the southwestern Blasted Lands, a cratered canyon filled with demons. After the Legion's defeat at Mount Hyjal, doomguard commander Lord Kazzak gathered wandering demons, doomguard, and felhounds under his banner. His dreadlord lieutenant, Razelikh the Defiler, directs the Shadowsworn cultists at the Altar of Storms and commands the local Dreadmaul ogres.",sp=0},{t="The Power of the Blood",b="Scholars and wanderers still brave the Blasted Lands in search of discoveries. Just inside the northern pass, Bloodmage Drazial and Bloodmage Lynnore experiment with organs from scorpids, basilisks, and boars. They use them to brew potent physical enhancers.\n\nFarther into the wastes, the draenei hermit Kum'isha seeks scattered draenethyst fragments, remnants of Draenor's shattered past. Travelers who recover them receive a reward from him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the ground red and barren?",a="The Blasted Lands were once part of the marshy Black Morass. The Dark Portal's raw demonic magic drained the region of life and moisture. When the Portal was destroyed, its searing heat and chaotic energies turned the clay into hard crimson earth.",al={"why is blasted lands red","why is it dead","what happened to the swamp"}},{q="What is the Dark Portal?",a="The Dark Portal is a massive gateway between Azeroth and Draenor, the sundered orcish homeworld now known as Outland. Though destroyed to sever the bridge between worlds, its great stone frame still stands under Nethergarde Keep's watch.",al={"where does dark portal go","is the portal open","what is the gateway"}},{q="Who controls Nethergarde Keep?",a="Nethergarde Keep is an Alliance bastion overseen by Kirin Tor mages and soldiers loyal to Stormwind. Built after the Second War under Archmage Khadgar's direction, it keeps a strict watch over the Dark Portal and repels nearby ogre and demon attacks.",al={"who runs nethergarde","is nethergarde alliance","nethergarde mages"}},{q="What is the Tainted Scar?",a="The Tainted Scar is a demon-filled canyon in the southern Blasted Lands. It shelters the remaining Burning Legion forces in the Eastern Kingdoms, led by the powerful doomguard Lord Kazzak and including doomguards, felguards, and felhounds.",al={"tainted scar elite area","who is in tainted scar","demon valley blasted lands"}},{q="Who are the blood elves camping near the entrance?",a="Bloodmage Drazial and Bloodmage Lynnore are researchers studying how the corrupted fauna adapted to the harsh fel landscape. They trade potent elixirs that bolster mortal attributes for entrails, brains, and lungs from native basilisks, vultures, scorpids, and boars.",al={"blood elf buff potions","drazial and lynnore","boar lung quest"}},{q="Who is Kum'isha the Collector?",a="Kum'isha is a draenei mystic who lives in the central wastes. He collects draenethyst fragments and spheres from Draenor, and trades sealed packs of rare equipment and goods to those who bring them to him.",al={"draenei in blasted lands","kumisha","draenethyst quest"}},{q="How do you reach the Blasted Lands on foot?",a="Travel through Deadwind Pass east into the Swamp of Sorrows. Follow the main road south past the Horde settlement of Stonard, then take the narrow mountain pass into the Blasted Lands.",al={"getting to blasted lands","how to get there","blasted lands entrance"}},{q="Why are there ogres living in the desert?",a="The Dreadmaul ogres crossed the Dark Portal during the Second War. They stayed instead of retreating through the rift, entrenched themselves in Dreadmaul Hold, and fell under the thrall of the dreadlord Razelikh and the Shadowsworn cult.",al={"dreadmaul ogres lore","why are ogres here","dreadmaul hold"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Nethergarde Keep's stern use of the arcane in its vigil against fel corruption and the dimensional rifts left by Medivh's fall.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can find powerful demons in the Tainted Scar, while Daio the Decrepit dwells among the rocks. The land offers seasoned warlocks rare chances to bind dangerous fel entities.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can find Gromsblood growing in the Blasted Lands' arid red clay, one of the few natural places where it grows.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can find your only fortified haven in the region at Nethergarde Keep. It guards the kingdom's southern reaches from threats to Duskwood and Stormwind.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde member, you can find no Horde fortress here. The Dark Portal's ruins remain a grim monument to the Old Horde's crossing and the devastation of demonic corruption."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dark portal","drazial","dreadmaul","gromsblood","kum'isha","lord kazzak","lynnore","nethergarde keep","razelikh","tainted scar"},rel={"subzone:dark-portal","subzone:nethergarde-keep","subzone:tainted-scar","zone:swampofsorrows","npc:bloodmage-drazial","npc:bloodmage-lynnore"},src={"Blasted Lands (Classic)","Blasted Lands"}}
